      "text": "We start with the given expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\cos 80^\\circ} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sin 80^\\circ}\n\\]\nTo combine these terms over a common denominator, we need to make the denominators the same. The common denominator is \\(\\cos 80^\\circ \\sin 80^\\circ\\). So, we rewrite the expression as:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sin 80^\\circ - \\sqrt{3} \\cos 80^\\circ}{\\cos 80^\\circ \\sin 80^\\circ}\n\\]\nNext, we use the angle addition formula for sine, which states that \\( \\sin(\\theta - \\phi) = \\sin \\theta \\cos \\phi - \\cos \\theta \\sin \\phi \\). By setting \\(\\theta = 45^\\circ\\) and \\(\\phi = 60^\\circ\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\sin(45^\\circ - 60^\\circ) = \\sin 45^\\circ \\cos 60^\\circ - \\cos 45^\\circ \\sin 60^\\circ\n\\]\nSince \\(\\sin 45^\\circ = \\cos 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\) and \\(\\cos 60^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2}\\) and \\(\\sin 60^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\), we substitute these values in:\n\\[\n\\sin 80^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} - \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6}}{4}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 80^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} + \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\]\nNow, we can substitute \\(\\sin 80^\\circ\\) and \\(\\cos 80^\\circ\\) back into the common denominator expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sin 80^\\circ - \\sqrt{3} \\cos 80^\\circ}{\\cos 80^\\circ \\sin 80^\\circ} = \\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6}}{4} - \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}}{\\frac{\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6}}{4} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}}\n\\]\nSimplify the numerator:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{3} (\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2})}{\\frac{(\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6})(\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2})}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{18} - \\sqrt{6}}{\\frac{(\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6})(\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2})}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6} - 3\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6}}{\\frac{(\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6})(\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2})}{4}}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{-2\\sqrt{2} - 2\\sqrt{6}}{\\frac{(\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6})(\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2})}{4}} = \\frac{-2(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6})}{\\frac{(\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6})(\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2})}{4}} = \\frac{-2(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6})}{\\frac{(\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2})}{4}} = \\frac{-2(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6})}{\\frac{(\\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2})}{4}}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{-2(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6})}{\\frac{(\\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2})}{4}} = \\frac{-2(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6})}{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2})}{4}} = \\frac{-8(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6})}{4(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{2})} = \\frac{-8(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6})}{4(\\sqrt{6})} = \\frac{-2(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6})}{\\sqrt{6}} = \\frac{-2(\\sqrt{6} + 2\\sqrt{2})}{\\sqrt{6}} = \\frac{-2\\sqrt{6} - 4\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{6}}\n\\]\nSince \\(\\frac{-2\\sqrt{6} - 4\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{6}}\\) simplifies to \\(\\frac{-2\\sqrt{6} - 4\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{6}} = -2\\sqrt{2} - 4\\], the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-2 \\sqrt{2} - 4}\n\\]",
